+      "text": "The 12 weeks ended September 5, 2026 and September 6, 2025 include volume outside of North America for the months of\n36\nTable of Contents\nJune, July and August. The 36 weeks ended September 5, 2026 and September 6, 2025 include volume outside of North America for the months of January through August.\nConsolidated Net Revenue and Operating Profit\n12 Weeks Ended 36 Weeks Ended\n9/5/2026 9/6/2025 Change 9/5/2026 9/6/2025 Change\nNet revenue $ 25,274 $ 23,937 6 % $ 68,898 $ 64,582 7 %\nOperating profit $ 4,260 $ 3,569 19 % $ 11,496 $ 7,941 45 %\nOperating margin 16.9 % 14.9 % 2.0 16.7 % 12.3 % 4.4\nSee “Results of Operations – Segment Review” for a tabular presentation and discussion of key drivers of net revenue.\n12 Weeks\nOperating profit increased 19%, primarily driven by productivity savings, a favorable net impact of acquisition and divestiture-related charges/credits, effective net pricing, a 4-percentage-point favorable impact of tariff refunds and a favorable impact of net mark-to-market gains on commodity derivatives. These impacts were partially offset by certain operating cost increases and higher advertising and marketing expenses.\n36 Weeks\nOperating profit increased 45%, primarily driven by productivity savings, prior-year impairment charges related to the Rockstar and Be & Cheery brands, effective net pricing and a favorable net impact of acquisition and divestiture-related charges/credits, partially offset by certain operating cost increases.\n",
